WEBVTT

00:00.080 --> 00:02.800
This is what a lot of drafts look like.

00:02.960 --> 00:06.000
Three versions of a word, split by slashes.

00:06.240 --> 00:07.600
A sentence written twice,

00:07.600 --> 00:09.040
because you couldn't decide.

00:09.360 --> 00:11.440
And at the bottom, everything you cut

00:11.440 --> 00:13.120
but couldn't bring yourself to delete.

00:13.835 --> 00:15.915
All of that deserves a better place.

00:16.449 --> 00:18.449
Here's the same draft with Vikalp.

00:18.849 --> 00:20.689
A thin underline and a few dots

00:20.689 --> 00:21.969
mean there are other versions.

00:22.684 --> 00:24.764
Hover over it and use the arrow keys,

00:24.764 --> 00:27.004
and you read each one right where it lives.

00:27.484 --> 00:29.004
There's no accept button.

00:29.004 --> 00:30.684
Whatever's showing is the note.

00:30.954 --> 00:33.354
This aside about lighthouses is nice,

00:33.354 --> 00:34.714
but it might not belong.

00:34.954 --> 00:37.149
Instead of deleting it, ghost it.

00:37.262 --> 00:40.382
Then there's the Lab, a few passes for editing.

00:40.542 --> 00:43.582
It can catch typos, mark the weakest sentences,

00:43.662 --> 00:46.942
the ones that run long, or words that don't fit the tone.

00:47.262 --> 00:48.462
Or ask it to tighten things

00:48.462 --> 00:49.662
up by about twenty percent.

00:51.359 --> 00:53.198
It doesn't rewrite a single sentence.

00:53.198 --> 00:54.238
It only strikes out the

00:54.238 --> 00:55.759
words it thinks you can lose.

00:55.839 --> 00:57.359
If it cuts something you'd keep,

00:57.359 --> 00:58.719
click it, and it stays.

00:59.038 --> 01:01.759
Then ghost the cuts, so nothing is gone for good.

01:02.091 --> 01:03.611
That's Vikalp.

01:03.611 --> 01:05.691
A writing plugin built for how you think.
